Hi,

This is a request to _open_ the TI developed Dynamic Object File
Format and other options to help community to make open doff loader in
userspace and to help make future dsp/iva gateway development easier.

Background:
=========

Dynamic Object File Format is a proprietary file format developed by
Texas Instruments. As per my knowledge of examining this file format,
it compresses the COFF file output generated by Code Composer Studio
and re-arranges the sections in to small packets, for which packets
size can be configured (by default looks like 1kB). It also removes
the debugging sections.

The direct benefit of using this format is the code loading time,
simple parsing and maintenance across the TI DSP architectures.

Option1:
=====

TI makes doff header files available to public, with sample doff
files. It is left to community to make parser and loader out of it.
Community generated code is available as GPL/LGPL or as selected by
the developer of it.

Most of multimedia companies I know of distributes their codecs in
this form it seems, so they can directly use this loader/parser to
test/develop the DSP/IVA gateway driver.

Option2:
======

Another option could be to make available coff header files with TI
changes for DSP CPU types #defines and other #ifdefers to public which
works with CCS3.1 or higher and also with OMAP2/3 generation of
processors having DSP and IVA1/2.

It is my observations that coff.h headers file used with CCS3.1 to
generate output files for IVA1 doesn't work to parse COFF output files
generated with N-DSPGW.

TI also makes available sample test coff file for community to develop
loader out of it.

Let me know if I am missing some points, as it is really getting hard
to scale the current dspgw design for asymmetric processors and
particularly integrate codecs delivered by multimedia companies with
open drivers/gateway.

